{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RnAVCbvzV4UzDXA3ew4cMx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, no syncing, plain-markdown source of truth).\n\n- **Purpose:** A personal task/project manager. Tasks, projects, inbox, and per-domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing) are stored as plain markdown and moved through a lifecycle (active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored).\n\n- **What it ships (the app):** `anchor_gui.py` â€” the declared deliverable. A self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server (port 8777) that renders the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes back to the markdown files via `/api/*` endpoints. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`.\n\n- **CLI mirror:** `anchor.py` reproduces the same logic as a command-line tool and generates the static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Reliability:** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM (Task Scheduler), parsing every file, booting a throwaway test server, exercising endpoints, walking a synthetic task through every state, and writing dated reports in `health_reports/`.\n\n- **The big add-on â€” an R&D control surface** (built across four versions, v4 \"Project Cockpit\" merged to master 2026-06-13): turns each project into a mission-control cockpit for \"trio\"-driven R&D work (Researchâ†’researchPrime Â· Planningâ†’Crucible Â· Buildâ†’Foreman). It ships:\n  - Per-project windows with lane tiles + status lights and inline-expanding panels.\n  - Real **ConPTY terminals** (the one waived dependency, optional `pywinpty`), each isolated in its own git worktree, with a stacking/accordion window manager.\n  - Cached, grounding-validated session and project **summaries**, per-lane doc-role maps, and cost/tokens/time rollups.\n  - A grass-idea board (promote to lane), engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), and type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port guaranteed â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render).\n  - Ghost World Labs branding (\"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\n- **Design discipline:** Python stdlib only (the lone declared exception is `pywinpty` for terminals), enforced by `distro.py`'s import scan; no database, no binary assets â€” everything stays readable/editable from any CLI tool.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: the bullets above describe what the docs/CLAUDE.md *claim* is shipped and merged. If you want, I can verify any specific claim (e.g., that v4 is actually on master, or that a given module/endpoint exists) against the live code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4397d641-8bd6-4893-b766-120b14ac9c80","uuid":"602198c1-66a1-4528-81a6-d113a1e17b1b","request_id":"req_011Cc1ha639ZqbcGrm5MJumm"}
